  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Given that the lines $y=5qx+9$ and $y=-3x-8$ are perpendicular, what is the value of $q?$",
  "worked_solution": "For the two lines to be perpendicular, their slopes must multiply to $-1.$\n\nBoth lines are slope-intercept form, and the slope is the $x$-coefficient. \n\n- The slope of the line $y=5qx+9$ is $5q.$\n\n- The slope of the line $y=-3x-8$ is $-3.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n5q\\cdot (-3)=-1\\,\u27f9\\,q=\\frac{1}{15}.\n$$",
